  "text": "She gave two coins and out-gave the entire treasury. Mark twelve. Jesus sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury. That is the setup. He sat down and watched people give. And many that were rich cast in much. Then comes a certain poor widow, and she throws in two mites, which make a farthing. Mark actually converts the currency for his readers, which tells you how small it was. And Jesus calls his disciples over, because he wants them to see this specifically. Verily I say unto you, that this poor widow hath cast more in, than all they which have cast into the treasury. More than all of them. And then he does the maths out loud. For all they did cast in of their abundance, but she of her want did cast in all that she had, even all her living. All her living. Not a percentage. The whole thing. He is not measuring the gift. He is measuring what was left afterwards.",
